  "question": {
    "text": "An electron projected perpendicular to a uniform magnetic field B moves in a circle. If Bohr's quantization is applicable, then the radius of the electronic orbit in the first excited state is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cOly5",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\pi \\mathrm{eB}}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "P0aOR",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{2 h}{\\pi e B}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CQdrB",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{h}{2 \\pi e B}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6PzLs",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{4 \\mathrm{~h}}{\\pi e B}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$m v r=\\frac{n h}{2 \\pi}$ ...(i)\n$r=\\frac{v m}{B q}$ ....(ii)\n$\\begin{aligned} & n=2 \\\\ & m r\\left(\\frac{r B q}{m}\\right)=\\frac{2 h}{2 \\pi} \\\\ & r=\\sqrt{\\frac{h}{\\pi B q}} \\\\ & q=e \\\\ & r=\\sqrt{\\frac{h}{\\pi B e}}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
